  "attempt": "For complex minor-arc terms w_k and any proxy v_k, define N_-(w)=sum_k max(-Re(w_k),0). Then N_-(w)<=N_-(v)+sum_k|w_k-v_k|. This follows because the negative-part map is one-Lipschitz after taking real parts. If only an l2 residual E is known, Cauchy-Schwarz gives the dimension-dependent bound N_-(w)<=N_-(v)+sqrt(m)E, and the factor sqrt(m) is sharp: m equal negative real residuals of size 1/sqrt(m) have l2 norm one and negative mass sqrt(m). Therefore an l2-only, dimension-free phase proxy cannot close the binary Goldbach signed-minor route.",
